.TH SSGRID 1 2000-1月 "sgrid_context" "sgrid_context"
.SH NAME
sgrid_context \- map a pseudobulk context(the raw expression counts) onto the model state space
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIsgrid_context(\fBnetwork\fR as <generic> SSystemNetwork, 
\fBx\fR as any, 
\fBmissing\fR as string = "baseline", 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
map a pseudobulk context(the raw expression counts) onto the model state space
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBnetwork\fB \fR\- -. 
.PP
.PP
\fBx\fB \fR\- 
 the pseudobulk context data, could be a csv file path, a data.frame(the 
 columns are \fBgene\fR and \fBmean_counts\fR), or a named numeric vector/list 
 (the names are the gene symbols, the values are the raw counts).
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmissing\fB \fR\- 
 the value that used for the genes which is missing in the given context: 
 \fBbaseline\fR(default) means the minimal value of that gene in the training 
 matrix, \fBzero\fR means the zero expression.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- -. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a named list of the model state space value, which can be used as the 
 \fBcontext\fR parameter of the \fBperturb\fR and \fBsgrid_simulate\fR api.
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
the model state is not the raw counts, but \fBlog2(max(counts,0)+pseudo) + delta\fR, 
 the per gene offset \fBdelta\fR was generated in the model fitting step. So the 
 pseudobulk context data must be transformed by this function before it can be 
 used as the ODE initial state.
.PP
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
let ctx = sgrid_context(network, "/data/pseudobulk_context_A.csv");
 let resp = perturb(network, genes, context = ctx);
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
ssGrid
.SH FILES
.PP
biosystem.dll
.PP
